<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Anthony Wayne</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1745">1745</a>–<a href="/years/1796">1796</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Anthony Wayne (1745–1796) was an American general, nicknamed &quot;Mad Anthony&quot; for his daring, who served in the Revolutionary War and captured Stony Point in 1779. Given command of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/legion">Legion</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a>, he defeated the Western Confederacy of Native nations at the Battle of Fallen <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timber">Timbers</a> in 1794 and negotiated the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-greenville">Treaty of Greenville</a> in 1795, which opened most of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ohio">Ohio</a> to American settlement.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/anthony-wayne.jpg" alt="Anthony Wayne" width="320" height="401" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: James Sharpless (c. 1795) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Anthony_Wayne,_uniform.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
